.TH geectl-remote-lock 1  "geectl-remote-lock 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-lock \- Lock a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the lock. A project lock records the message on the lock; a package lock sends it but the server does not record it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote lock\fR [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> [\fIPACKAGE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lock a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the lock. A project lock records the message on the lock; a package lock sends it but the server does not record it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR
A message for the lock. A project lock records it; a package lock\*(Aqs message is not recorded — there is no package\-scope lock command
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to lock
.TP
[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
The package to lock. Omit to lock the whole project
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
